From naomi at stat.psu.edu  Mon May 16 18:15:14 2011
From: naomi at stat.psu.edu (Naomi Altman)
Date: Mon, 16 May 2011 12:15:14 -0400
Subject: [BioC] about limma linear models
In-Reply-To: <1cada06.9613.12ff89b74e1.Coremail.sense_0109@126.com>
References: <1cada06.9613.12ff89b74e1.Coremail.sense_0109@126.com>
Message-ID: <6.2.3.4.1.20110516121304.05e56a08@imap.stat.psu.edu>

If you have biological replicates, then using LIMMA is preferred with 
small sample sizes.  If you have only technical replicates, then you 
really cannot do a proper statistical analysis of the data.  Since 
you have a disconnected design, you might use separate channel 
analysis to simplify the comparisons you want to make.

Regards,
Naomi Altman


