You are missing the fact that the fold changes that siggenes reports are 
no longer on the log scale.

 > 2^(9.68-10.55)
[1] 0.5471469
 > 2^(9.02-5.18)
[1] 14.3204
 > 2^(6.15-1.91)
[1] 18.89588

My values are slightly off because IIRC, what really happens in siggenes 
(and for sure happens in SAM) is that the data are 'unlogged' first, 
then the mean is computed, then the ratio.

